Joe wrote:
> So I always have a bunch of scrolls with gibberish titles.  Is the main way
> to identify these with an identify scroll?  If so, will I know an identify
> scroll when I see it?  I've played 10 or so characters, and have found no
> way to identify items.  I generally only get as far as Dlvl 4, but once I
> got to the mines level 8 - do I find identify scrolls much later?

You won't know a scroll of identify from its gibberish name, you have to
identify these by yourself.

Scrolls of identify are the cheepest scrolls existing. So if you not want
to unknowingly read them - which is wise, BTW - you need to find some shop
(general purpose, or paper ware); sell them and you are offered around 10
zorkmids. If you find a shop with a scroll worth somewhat around 20 zorkmids
it's likely a scroll of identify.

There are other means to identify items, but most of them are accessible in
the late game (a spellbook of identify, divine help, ...)

